(see bullets 1-3).
















We now check that $G=K_{n_2}$ by determining there is exactly one edge between each pair of vertices in $v_i,v_j\in V(G)$.
For $v_i,v_j\in V_N$, where $v_i,v_j\in \phi^{-1}(y_p)$ for $y_p \in Y$, by (iii) and (vi), $\ell_{G'}(y_p)= 1+\left(\frac{b(b-1)}{2}-1\right)=\frac{b(b-1)}{2}={b \choose 2}={\eta(y_p)\choose 2}$. By Theorem \ref{amalgamationtheorem} (ii), $m_G(v_i,v_j)=\ell_{G'}(y_p)/{\eta(y_p)\choose 2}={\eta(y_p)\choose 2}/{\eta(y_p)\choose 2}=1$. Checking this for all other $v_i,v_j\in V(G)$ is the same as Case 1 (see bullets 5-7).

